{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Eloise >:3c","id":"260820438026813440","is_bot":0,"username":"effervescenteloise"},"author_id":"260820438026813440","channel_id":"636014580690321428","content":"(so I wrote a piece of fanfic as one of Daysong's journal entries. <@313689699627696139> enjoy:)\nI saw my own death today. Again. The image becomes increasingly clear as we move closer, as possible variations are eliminated and the future solidifies itself. But it does not bring me grief. Because for the first time, I saw beyond that. I saw the second marriage of little Anansi, and the dreams that three of my siblings will have that night. It is no small comfort to see all the faces I saw, and know that they will make it through the trial I do not. \nThey will all three of them dream of history. I cannot see the fine details yet, as dreams are fickle things. I know that he will dream of beginnings, of cornerstones and Pym. I see that she will dream of the future, of all the great footsteps she is sure to fill. I feel that they will dream of victory, and its costs. I see that they will need this dream, to keep their resolve. \nI see also that Ebuc will live on, in a way. More so than memory. I see the things that made Ebuc strong and kind and I see them in his creation. \nI can see the moment that my right hand learns of my passing. In some strange certainty I can see her face perfectly clear. That moment is etched in time's stone. But I see too how strong she has become. \nI see the mold, and Hiram's work begginning to be rediscovered. \nBut the thing that brings me the most joy, out of all of this, is Little Anansi's face when they learn the chisel's true nature. That shock, that wonder, that disbelief. That makes everything worth it.","created_at":"2020-08-09T09:24:04.374000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"741949914476707850","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
